---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import RecipeCard from '../../components/RecipeCard.astro'

const macro = `defaults:
  who: sam@example.com
steps:
  - fill: { label: Email }
    value: $who
  - click: { role: button, name: Sign in }`

const use = `setup:
  - use: sign-in
  - use: sign-in
    with: { who: admin@example.com }`

const data = `setup:
  - each: $orders
    as: order
    steps:
      - click: { text: '\${order.name}' }`
---

<Docs
  title="Macros and data"
  description="Sharing setup between recipes, and driving one from a list."
>
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold">Macros and data</h1>

  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    Setup shared between recipes goes in <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">paths.macros</code
    >, one file per macro. The filename is its name.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={macro} file="screenshots/macros/sign-in.yaml" />
  </div>
  <div class="mt-4">
    <RecipeCard code={use} file="screenshots/recipes/dashboard.yaml" />
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Data files</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    Files in <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">paths.data</code> are in scope by filename:
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">screenshots/data/orders.yaml</code> is
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">$orders</code>, and
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">each: $orders</code> iterates it.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={data} file="screenshots/recipes/orders.yaml" />
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    The filename becomes a <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">$name</code>, so keep it to
    letters, digits and underscores — a <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">$</code> reference stops
    at a hyphen, and <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">open-orders.yaml</code> cannot be reached.
    Group what would have been several hyphenated files into one and read them by path:
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">$orders.open</code>,
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">$orders.shipped</code>.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    A reference reads what the data holds and nothing else. Keys that belong to the language —
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">__proto__</code>,
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">constructor</code>,
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">prototype</code> — resolve to nothing, and a reference that
    matches nothing is an error rather than an empty string. A literal
    <code class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">$</code> inside a longer string is left alone, so a shot
    of "costs $5" survives.
  </p>
</Docs>
